The original ticket's claim that one parser fix covers every report is not supported by this export.
Counts describe the 2026-10-04 export. The later desk engineering update is recorded below; it supplies dispositions, not new report counts.

<ReportSplit />

## Separate the evidence before assigning fixes

Use tenant locale and booking-form version, rather than browser locale or intake tags, to distinguish
the shared month-first parser from booking-v3's month-first hint on a day-first form. Deduplicate by
report ID; matching subjects alone do not establish a shared cause.

The desk's oneDayMove list contradicts its parser attribution. R-41202, R-41209, R-41344 and R-41620
describe one-day discrepancies. R-41236 instead says the invite arrived before the booking and
needs its own chronology investigation. No timezone root cause has been demonstrated.

The five exceptions remain part of the original ticket's mechanically computed parser group;
the parser issue retains all 379 reports, while the hint issue covers 33. The four one-day reports
and one chronology report are overlapping investigation subsets, not additional reports.
379 + 33 = 412 unique reports. The auxiliary disjoint triage view is 374/33/4/1; it is not the desk's issue count
and does not prove four independent root causes.

## Desk disposition — 5 October

The Challenge-page engineering update, supplied by the student, says #4471 closed on 5 October:

- Parser: **fixed** — `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- Hint: **won’t fix** — booking-v3 form retired.

This is desk-reported status; no fix commit URL or runtime verification was supplied.
The four one-day discrepancies and the chronology report still have unconfirmed causes.
Their overlapping tracking issues were closed as not planned to consolidate this course triage;
that does not establish that those symptoms were fixed.

## Evidence and follow-up

[Report bodies, ID mapping and reproducible analysis](https://github.com/kriss94/mega/tree/main/s01e03/reports)
are preserved alongside the export. Run `node s01e03/analyze.mjs` at the repository root to verify
counts. The product itself has not been run, and the export contains no package manifest for a KB build.

Obtain original event timestamps and timezone settings for the discrepant reports. Recheck desk
updates before claiming a current total or resolution. The accepted subject-only dedupe decision
is preserved; replacing it requires a new decision record.


